## Router delegation

- Use the `dispatch` skill when work splits cleanly, fits a four-line brief, has
  an independent verifier, and is worth the extra model calls.
- Every brief has TASK, FILES, BAR, and RETURN. Workers return five lines:
  CHANGED / BAR / OUTPUT / NOT DONE / OPEN.
- Send evidence sweeps to `seat-sweep` (Haiku), bounded builds to `seat-exec`
  (Sonnet, its own worktree), and every return to a fresh `seat-judge` (Opus).
- Let the router choose the model and tier. The judge reads the actual work,
  re-runs the BAR, returns PASS or SEND_BACK, and never fixes it.
- Retry a failed execution brief on Sonnet once. Next use `route: up ladder`
  for one Opus attempt. After that, return the unresolved brief to the owner.
- Keep FILES narrow, preserve unrelated work, and never include secrets in returns.
- `router off` disables the hooks; `router on` enables them again.
